   "source": [
    "<a name=\"sec3_3\"></a>\n",
    "### 3.3 Summary Findings & Next Steps\n",
    "- OpenXML structural tags (`struct_pos`, `struct_typeface`, `path_a-hlink`) provide near-perfect discriminative power.\n",
    "- Zero-imputation appropriately captured legacy file format characteristics.\n",
    "- Models will be trained with `StandardScaler` to put features on uniform scale.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<a name=\"sec4\"></a>\n",
    "## 4. Preprocessing and Feature Creation\n",
    "Construct log-transformed attributes and standardized arrays.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-03T09:53:17.913350Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-03T09:53:17.912349Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-03T09:53:17.921652Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-03T09:53:17.921652Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Engineered log features added. Feature count: 14 attributes.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Preprocessing: engineer log-transformed attributes\n",
    "train_proc = train.copy()\n",
    "test_proc = test.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "for col in [\"path_a-hlink\", \"struct_name\", \"path_a-alpha\", \"struct_script\"]:\n",
    "    train_proc[f\"{col}_log\"] = np.log1p(train_proc[col])\n",
    "    test_proc[f\"{col}_log\"] = np.log1p(test_proc[col])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Engineered log features added. Feature count: {train_proc.shape[1] - 2} attributes.\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<a name=\"sec5\"></a>\n",
